{% comment %}
  snippet: gl-tech-bool.liquid
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Renders one Technical data value with consistent casing.

  The yes/no rows on the product page are `single_line_text_field` metafields
  fed by Sales Layer, so the same answer arrives spelled several ways — "SI",
  "Si", "Yes", "No", "NO", "Opcional", "OPCIONAL" — and each language has its
  own stored value. Printing them raw put two or three casings in one table.

  This uppercases a value ONLY when it is one of those yes/no/optional words.
  Everything else is passed through exactly as stored, so real values such as
  "FLASH HIDER", "SUB-MOA", "Carril Picatinny" or a choke name are untouched.

  The wording itself is Sales Layer's to own — this changes presentation only,
  never the word.

  Usage:
    {% render 'gl-tech-bool', value: product.metafields.custom.rosca.value %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign raw = value | strip
  assign probe = raw | downcase

  comment
    Every spelling Sales Layer currently sends across both languages.
    "optinal" is theirs, misspelt at source; it is listed so it is at least
    cased like its neighbours, and is deliberately not corrected here.
  endcomment
  assign bool_words = 'si,sí,no,yes,opcional,optional,optinal' | split: ','

  if raw == blank
    echo '—'
  elsif bool_words contains probe
    echo raw | upcase
  else
    echo raw
  endif
-%}
